{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Card","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.contig_no_triangle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.contig_no_triangle","kind":"theorem","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L304-L313","doc":"**No 3-cell on the contiguous layout**, as a corollary of the above rather\nthan as a hypothesis about the graph. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.contig_bonded_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.contig_bonded_iff","kind":"theorem","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L296-L302","doc":"**The contiguous layout is a chain.**  Blocks `j` and `k` are bonded exactly\nwhen they are consecutive — degree at most two, no triangle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.contig_disjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.contig_disjoint","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L290-L294","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.contig_internal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.contig_internal","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L288-L288","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.contigBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.contigBlock","kind":"def","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L285-L286","doc":"Block `k` of the contiguous layout: strands `{3k, 3k+1, 3k+2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.residue_layout_is_the_excluded_triangle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.residue_layout_is_the_excluded_triangle","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L273-L281","doc":"Packaged: the interleaved layout carries a triangle **and** is γγ-excluded.\nThe two halves together are the statement that the γγ demand, not the braid\ngroup, is what removes the 3-cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.residue_block_not_internal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.residue_block_not_internal","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L262-L271","doc":"**But no interleaved block admits an internal γγ vertex.**  By\n`eq_triple_of_internal` such a block would be a run of three consecutive\nstrands; an interleaved block contains no two consecutive strands at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.residue_layout_bonded_pairwise","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.residue_layout_bonded_pairwise","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L253-L260","doc":"**The interleaved layout's coordination graph is a triangle.**  Each pair of\nblocks is bonded, including the wrap-around pair `{2,5,8}`–`{0,3,6}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.residue_disjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.residue_disjoint","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L245-L251","doc":"The three interleaved blocks are pairwise disjoint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.card_residueBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.card_residueBlock","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L240-L243","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.mem_residueBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.mem_residueBlock","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L236-L238","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.residueBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.residueBlock","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L232-L234","doc":"Block `k` of the interleaved (\"residue\") layout at `A = 3`: strands\n`{k, k+3, k+6}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.degree_le_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.degree_le_two","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L210-L222","doc":"A block's neighbours among disjoint triples number at most two — the bases\n`a - 3` and `a + 3`.  Stated as: three pairwise-distinct triples all bonded to\n`triple a` and pairwise disjoint from it cannot exist. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.no_triangle_of_triples","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.no_triangle_of_triples","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L192-L208","doc":"**No triangle.**  Three pairwise-disjoint triples cannot be pairwise\nbonded: bonding forces each pair of bases to differ by exactly `3`, and three\ndistinct naturals cannot pairwise differ by `3`.\n\nThis is the `Finset ℕ` analogue of `NoThreeCellOnTheChain.no_triangle`, reached\nfrom the γγ vertex instead of from a `LinearLayout` hypothesis.  The two are\nindependent routes to the same conclusion; neither is derived from the other\n(see the 🛑 note at the top). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.bonded_iff_base_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.bonded_iff_base_succ","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L176-L188","doc":"**Two disjoint triples are bonded iff their bases differ by exactly three.**\n\nA block's only possible neighbours are the triples immediately to its left and\nright — which is why the coordination graph is a path. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.triple_disjoint_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.triple_disjoint_iff","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L155-L174","doc":"Disjointness of two triples, read on their bases. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.internal_iff_isTriple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.internal_iff_isTriple","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L146-L151","doc":"Restated as an equivalence on three-strand blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.internal_triple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.internal_triple","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L141-L144","doc":"The converse: an interval *does* admit an internal vertex, so `Internal` is\nnot vacuously false and `eq_triple_of_internal` is not an empty implication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.eq_triple_of_internal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.eq_triple_of_internal","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L130-L139","doc":"**A three-strand block admitting an internal γγ vertex IS an interval.**\n\nThis is the whole structural content: the vertex's own support already has\nthree elements, so a three-element block containing it *equals* it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.mem_triple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.mem_triple","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L127-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.card_triple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.card_triple","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L122-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.bonded_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.bonded_symm","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L115-L118","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.Bonded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.Bonded","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L109-L113","doc":"Two blocks are **bonded** when some strand of one is the immediate\nsuccessor of a strand of the other.  This is exactly an edge of the strand\npath `s — (s+1)` crossing between the two blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.Internal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.Internal","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L104-L107","doc":"A block is **γγ-internal** when some pair-production vertex lies entirely\ninside it — i.e. the nucleon can braid itself without reaching another\nnucleon's strand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.vertexStrands_eq_triple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.vertexStrands_eq_triple","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.triple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.triple","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L99-L100","doc":"A run of three consecutive strands based at `a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.vertexStrands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.vertexStrands","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/GammaGammaForcesTheLayout.lean#L95-L97","doc":"The three strands the γγ vertex `σᵢ σᵢ₊₁⁻¹` touches.  `σⱼ` exchanges\nstrands `j` and `j+1`, and the vertex uses generators `i` and `i+1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}